   "src": "L8274-8276,L8305-8307",
   "text": "The contests take place near the Tree of Life, with care not to damage its roots, waterways, nearby wildlife or ritual grounds. A critic who demands that beauty justify itself is about to meet a village that disagrees.\nA child-sized carved guardian is spectacularly ugly, with uneven eyes, three chins and a grin that looks painfully sincere. The master carver calls it \"an insult to wood.\" Villagers begin leaving flowers beside it.",
